    "final_answer": "I have all the information needed to answer the task. Let me provide a clear summary of the gluten-free brownie recipe found on Allrecipes.\n\n## Recipe Found: Gluten-Free Fudge Brownies\n\n**Rating & Reviews:**\n- ⭐ **4.1 out of 5 stars**\n- **76 Ratings** / **59 Reviews** (well above the 50-review threshold)\n\n**Time:**\n- **Prep Time:** 15 minutes\n- **Cook Time:** 45 minutes\n- **Total Time: 1 hour**\n- **Yield:** 16 brownies\n\n**Main Ingredients:**\n1. ⅔ cup gluten-free baking mix (such as Bob's Red Mill All Purpose GF Baking Flour®)\n2. ½ cup cornstarch\n3. 1 cup white sugar\n4. 1 cup packed brown sugar\n5. ¾ cup unsweetened cocoa powder\n6. 1 teaspoon baking soda\n7. 2 eggs, beaten\n8. ¾ cup margarine, melted\n\n**Description:** \"Celiacs will love this gluten-free version of fudge brownies. It's made of basic ingredients, and the flour mix is widely available in grocery stores.\"\n\n**Brief Directions:** Preheat oven to 350°F (175°C), and grease an 8x8-inch square baking dish. Stir together the gluten-free baking mix, cornstarch, white sugar, brown sugar, cocoa powder, and baking soda in a bowl, sifting with a fork to remove lumps. Pour in the eggs and melted margarine, and mix with a large spoon or electric mixer on low until the mixture forms a smooth batter (3 to 5 minutes). Scrape the batter into the prepared baking dish. Place a sheet of aluminum foil on the oven rack to prevent spills, then bake until a toothpick inserted in the center comes out clean (40 to 45 minutes).\n\n**Nutrition per serving:** 228 calories, 10g fat, 36g carbs, 3g protein\n\nThis recipe fully meets all the task requirements — it's a high-rated gluten-free brownie recipe with over 50 reviews.",
